DESCRIPTION:<b>REGISTRATION</b>: <a href="https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pa
 ges/ResponsePage.aspx?id=TsVyyzFKnk2xSh6jbfrJTI9QJhcY12JAolV5CeByrWpUQTNU
 ME1WQjlNR0JNSzROT1FBR1JRSUpESC4u" target="_blank">Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NO
 TE: Registration closes 24 hours before event start. Please register ahea
 d of the event. Registrants will receive Zoom information and related mat
 erials by email one week and within 24 hours before the event.</i>\n\nRes
 erve your seat in the virtual Research Integrity Roundtable <i>Mentorship
  and Research Integrity: Discussions for mentors and mentees</i> on May 2
 1\, 2026 from 8:30am - 10:00am. Participants will learn about why good me
 ntorship is important\, crucial components of mentorship in research\, an
 d tips to combat insufficient mentorship for mentors and mentees. Partici
 pants will discuss a case study related to a mentorship dilemma in small 
 groups and as a large group.\n\nThis event is only open to current Duke f
 aculty\, staff\, and students. Participation in this event fulfills the <
 b>RCR-200</b> requirement for Faculty and Staff\, the <b>200-level NSF RE
 CR</b> requirement\, and the <b>715 RCR credit</b> for graduate students.
  Participants must attend for 60 minutes and participate in breakout room
  discussion to receive credit.\n\nFor more information on the NSF RECR tr
 aining requirement please see the <a href="https://myresearchpath.duke.ed
 u/nsf-responsible-and-ethical-conduct-research-recr-training" target="_bl
 ank">myRESEARCHpath page</a>.
DURATION:PT1H30M
